# Environment for remote-terminal-agent.service. Read after the unit's own
# Environment= lines, so anything set here wins.
#
# This file is for the machine, not for the agent's behaviour: relay URL,
# token, limits and shells all live in /etc/remote-terminal-agent/config.json.

# Write a rotating agent.log under /var/log/remote-terminal-agent as well as
# the journal. Worth doing where the journal is volatile (Storage=volatile) or
# small, since a month-old disconnect is exactly what you want to look up.
#LOG_TO_FILE=1
#LOG_MAX_BYTES=5242880
#LOG_MAX_FILES=5

# error | warn | info | debug. debug logs every relay message type and every
# session lifecycle event; it never logs terminal contents or tokens.
#LOG_LEVEL=info

# Where terminals start. Defaults to the service user's home.
#SHELL_CWD=/var/lib/remote-terminal-agent

# Set to 1 to pass this unit's whole environment to the shells it opens.
# Off by default: a shell should not inherit a service manager's environment.
#INHERIT_ENV=0
